lation depends heavily on the AIR's dimensions—with num_cosets, num_x_blocks, and block_x all multiplying together, the actual buffer size could be much larger than I initially thought.\n\nRather than chase down the exact memory breakdown, I should just cap the intermediates budget at 64 MB to stay within L2 cache limits and batch only the AIRs that fit within that constraint.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":146045,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":342},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa62649b-653a-4cec-aa74-3431ae869005","uuid":"fd9522dd-82cc-4462-9d75-b4ddc6591710"}
