{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013GC4JfZ7Q5aD81MhEWjWxz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The zerocheck batch kernel hangs by itself (without logup batch). Even the smaller group (43 AIRs with num_cosets=1) is included. Let me try batching just a single small group to narrow down the issue.\n\nActually, let me look at the problem from a different angle. The kernels launched are:\n1. `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` (eval)\n2. `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` (reduction)\n\nBoth are launched for each group. The hang could be in either.\n\n\nI need to isolate which kernel is causing the hang. Since both the eval and reduce kernels are launched together in a single FFI call to `batched_zerocheck_r0_eval_constraints`, I'll need to refactor that call to add a synchronization point between them so I can pinpoint where execution stalls.\n\nActually, the quickest way to diagnose this is to test with just a single AIR instead of the full batch—if one AIR hangs, the kernel logic itself is broken, but if it works fine and only fails with 43+ AIRs, that points to a scaling or resource contention issue. Let me modify the batching logic to test with just one AIR first.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":135,"cache_read_input_tokens":191333,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":135},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa62649b-653a-4cec-aa74-3431ae869005","uuid":"5c22b89f-5895-4b92-98e6-5fb4b72a9553"}
