{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PKDp5xPJiVJm2ZfNhU9a8q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017NNW1XdJW8DYoascGxeP1X","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nRe-enable batch Round 0 descriptor-array kernels for small AIRs\n\nAdd batched CUDA kernels and Rust orchestration for batching small\ncoset-parallel AIRs in Round 0. Design: eval-only on default stream\nbefore Phase 2, with extraction deferred to worker threads.\n\nCUDA changes:\n- batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel: descriptor-array eval\n- batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel: same pattern for logup\n- FFI structs: Round0BlockCtx, Round0ZcCtx, Round0LogupCtx\n\nRust changes:\n- New round0_batched.rs: identify_batchable_airs(), batch_round0_eval_only(),\n  extract_batched_air(), with L2 cache budget (64 MB aggregate limit)\n- Integration in mod.rs: batch eval before Phase 2, worker thread routing\n\nNote: This optimization has a known CUDA kernel bug causing GPU hangs\nwhen >12 AIRs are batched (kernel never completes, GPU at 100%).\nWill be reverted in the next commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit implementation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":202,"cache_read_input_tokens":218986,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":202},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa62649b-653a-4cec-aa74-3431ae869005","uuid":"e7d191c6-81a1-4baf-a322-3bba75ae9fc4"}
